WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.042
Daily repairs are grouped as return repairs, in progress,
waiting for parts and waiting for collection.

00:00:06.042 --> 00:00:11.083
Use the search field to find a customer, device or order, then
check the device.

00:00:11.083 --> 00:00:13.333
Click the stage badge in the order row.

00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:21.250
In the window, choose the actual progress, such as awaiting
diagnosis, being repaired, or repaired and waiting for
collection.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:26.125
Check the stage, add a reason when required, then click the
save button below.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:31.083
A stage change does not confirm parts arrival, payment or the
return of the device.

00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:33.125
Open contact and follow-up.

00:00:33.125 --> 00:00:37.750
Choose quote discussed, contact unsuccessful, or awaiting a
reply.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:41.500
No written note is required; earlier notes remain in history.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.250
After selecting, press Record result.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.000
Record only contact that actually occurred.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.250
It does not confirm repair consent, send messages, or change
the repair stage.
